{"type":"message","id":"09567ca7","parentId":"aae13f2a","timestamp":"2026-02-17T17:29:53.678Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Tue 2026-02-17 22:59 GMT+5:30] Implement the safest stability fixes from the root cause analysis, with backup and rollback.\n\n**Goal**: Improve gateway stability and reduce rate limit disruptions with minimal risk.\n\n**Safe fixes to apply (in order):**\n\n1. **WebSocket keepalive tuning** — add ping/pong intervals to prevent NAT timeouts\n   - Locate WebSocket server creation (likely in `dist/entry.js` or `src/ws-server.ts`)\n   - Set: `pingInterval: 30000`, `pingTimeout: 10000`\n   - This is low-risk and often helps\n\n2. **OpenRouter retry/backoff** — handle 429 responses gracefully\n   - Find OpenRouter provider code: `src/providers/openrouter.ts` or similar\n   - Add: detect 429, read `Retry-After` header, exponential backoff with jitter\n   - Also add config: `models.providers.openrouter.maxRetries: 3` and `backoffMs: 1000`\n   - This may require careful editing but is contained to one provider\n\n3. **Gateway lock cleanup** — make startup more robust\n   - Review lock handling code (likely `src/gateway/lock.ts` or similar)\n   - On startup, check if lock PID is still running; if not, auto-clear\n   - This prevents stale lock delays\n\n**Before making changes:**\n- Create a backup of the current config and affected source files\n- Document what will be changed and why\n- Prepare rollback steps (git revert or restore backups)\n\n**Regarding model backup/alternatives:**\n- Add these free models to the models catalog as potential alternatives: `arcee-ai/trinity-large-preview:free`, `deepseek/deepseek-r1-0528:free`, `z-ai/glm-4.5-air:free`, `openai/gpt-oss-120b:free`\n- Update agent configs to include these as fallback options (not switch primary yet)\n- Design a simple automatic failover: when 429 occurs, switch to another free model from the list for subsequent requests\n\n**Deliverables:**\n1. Summary of changes made\n2. File diffs or descriptions\n3. Verification steps to confirm fixes are working\n4. Any config updates needed to enable/disable features\n\n**Caution:** Only apply changes that are clearly reversible and well-understood. If any change requires complex modifications or could break running services, skip it and report why. Prioritize stability over completeness.\n\nWork in the OpenClaw project at `D:\\workspace\\appDev\\openclaw`. Use your best judgment and be meticulous."}],"timestamp":1771349393675}}
{"type":"message","id":"7a9d78c3","parentId":"09567ca7","timestamp":"2026-02-17T17:29:58.407Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is a comprehensive task to implement stability fixes for the OpenClaw gateway. Let me break down what needs to be done:\n\n1. **WebSocket keepalive tuning** - add ping/pong intervals\n2. **OpenRouter retry/backoff** - handle 429 responses gracefully\n3. **Gateway lock cleanup** - make startup more robust\n4. **Model backup/alternatives** - add free models as fallback options\n\nThe task emphasizes safety, backup, and rollback. I need to:\n- Create backups before making changes\n- Document changes and why\n- Prepare rollback steps\n- Apply changes in order (lowest risk first)\n- Only apply changes that are clearly reversible\n\nLet me start by exploring the codebase to understand the structure and locate the relevant files.\n\nFirst, I should list the project structure to understand where things are.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"I'll implement the safest stability fixes with proper backup and rollback procedures. Let me start by exploring the codebase to locate the relevant files and understand the current implementation."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_6487d3f8bedf411e945b1579","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"ls -la"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free","usage":{"input":13664,"output":450,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":14114,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1771349393678}}
